// One receiver's per-sender cache for one peer: initialize, replace, restart,
// refill, cached, miss. The earlier formulation put the content in the state
// fact (Cache(s,r,d,e,incarnation)) and left every guarantee to be stated over
// actions. That was unprovable here: an action-level goal whose subject appears
// only in action facts and in facts with varying arguments gives induction
// nothing to follow.
//
// A trace formula can only refer to action facts. The manual is explicit: the
// application of a rule "is recorded in the trace by appending the instantiated
// action facts", and a trace property is a guarded first-order formula "over
// action facts and timepoints". Measured on two-rule theories (Tamarin 1.12.0,
// every verdict at exit 0): a fact that appears only in a rule's premises and
// conclusions is observable at NO index - not at its creating step, not at its
// consuming step, not at an unrelated later step. That holds for persistent
// facts too: a never-consumed !Keep(x) has no index at which it is observable.
// So any statement over "Slot(s,r,st,inc) @t" or "Content(s,r,d,e) @t" holds
// vacuously. This file used to rest on such statements; they are gone, and the
// earlier claim that a fact is "observable strictly between the steps that
// create and consume it" was wrong - there is no such window.
//
// The state is made trace-relevant by observing it: every rule that acts on a
// slot emits SlotObs(sender,receiver,'held'|'empty',incarnation) for the state
// it consumes and, where it changes, the state it leaves. Premises, conclusions
// and Out facts are unchanged, so the transition system, the reachable states
// and the adversary's knowledge are exactly as before; only observations are
// added. Every lemma is then stated over actions, and the bridges below tie
// each action to the state it acted on at its own step.
//
// One consequence to keep in mind: restart emits held and empty for the same
// incarnation at one step, which is legitimate - that step is where held
// becomes empty. An invariant forbidding that pair is therefore FALSE: checked,
// both "one slot never reports both states" and "never empty then held" read
// over SlotObs are refuted. The true statement is directional - an incarnation
// observed empty is never observed held at a LATER step.
//
// Verified (see the order below: every [reuse] source precedes what uses it):
// each cache action occurs at a step observing the state it names (the
// current/empty/ended/started/resolved bridges, 3-9 steps); those observations
// really occur, including a held one followed later by an empty one (three
// witnesses); a cached resolution, a restart then a miss; an incarnation start for
// one pair is unique; every observation of a slot holding an incarnation traces to
// a start of it at or before that step, hence an end action traces to an earlier
// start; a current action traces to an earlier start; a miss records an earlier
// end; an end is observed holding and is followed at the same step by empty; a
// resolution traces to an earlier delivery; a refill follows the restart that
// emptied the slot.
// Open at 8 GiB, exit 137 (a cgroup kill, not a timeout) at every budget tried
// from 400 to 1300 seconds, and none is refuted:
// - the two forms of "an incarnation observed empty or ended is never observed
//   held again" (no_held_obs_after_empty, no_held_obs_after_end). Each verifies
//   ONLY when the other stands above it as a [reuse] source; with neither
//   assumed both exhaust the search. That is circular, so neither is a proof:
//   [reuse] injects a lemma's statement into later proofs whether or not that
//   lemma was proved, and in per-lemma mode an earlier [reuse] lemma is never
//   attempted in the same process, so it is only ever an assumption. Both are
//   now without [reuse] and reported open, so that nothing below can assume them.
// - the two consequences that used to read them as sources
//   (empty_incarnation_not_current_afterward, cache_incarnation_active). A
//   contrapositive shape (positive observation at the induction index, negated
//   existential) and an adjacency-bounded shape were both tried on these and
//   exhausted the search too.
// - no_resolution_after_restart_without_refill, and restart_refill_resolves_
//   witness (its restart -> refill half verifies alone; its refill -> resolution
//   half does not).
// [use_induction] was added to restart_refill_resolves_witness in case the
// admission theories' fix applied here; it did not (137 at 500 s), and an
// exists-trace has no induction to steer. Confined restatements of the
// resolution goals (delivery between restart and resolution; the delivery a
// resolution rests on with no restart in between; the same keyed on the empty
// observation) and a witness with the principals pinned to constants all
// exhausted the search too.
// Antecedent reachability of these six, from generated probes
// their antecedents are satisfiable, asserted in this file as
// Nonvac_no_held_obs_after_empty and Nonvac_no_held_obs_after_end (generated by
// contrib/ci/vacuity-probes.py: exists-trace of the antecedent alone, the
// conclusion's ordering removed):
// the other three probes exhaust the limit (exit 137 at 8 GiB, 100-550 s), so
// those three remain of unknown status rather than known-vacuous. (Five probes:
// the restart -> refill -> resolution witness has no antecedent to probe.) A probe that
// does not finish is not evidence of vacuity, exactly as a failed proof is not
// evidence of falsity.
// All six open goals have the same shape: a claim about a
// chain of observations whose induction step is the gap between two adjacent
// observations, which no statement here names. Closing them needs that stronger
// simultaneous induction, not more time or memory. A single combined form with a
// disjunctive antecedent does not parse: unguarded #i.
// One statement that had been open at every limit tried closed by restating it,
// not by raising limits: refill_follows_restart quantified over two starts and
// never named the refill step, so the search had to consider every pair of starts
// in every interleaving; the confined form (refill_follows_prior_restart) puts
// that one action in the antecedent and verifies in 141 seconds.
// Lemma order is part of a result here: with [reuse], a lemma may only use
// sources written above it, and this file's order is chosen so each chain lemma
// follows its sources. Do not reorder without re-running.
//
// Proof skeletons do parse in this version, but not the way the manual's prose
// suggests: a skeleton is a BARE method chain after the formula (simplify /
// solve( Fact( args ) @ #t ) / case rule / SOLVED / qed); 'by' is only a
// complete standalone suffix form, which is why 'by solve( ... )' fails to
// parse while 'by sorry' does. Forcing the action -> rule case split that way
// was tried on two of the open goals above and did not close them.
theory peer_cache
begin
builtins: hashing

restriction UniqueCache:
  "All s r #i #j. Initialized(s,r) @i & Initialized(s,r) @j ==> #i = #j"

rule initialize:
  [ Fr(~delegation), Fr(~epochs), Fr(~incarnation) ]
  --[ Initialized($sender,$receiver), Full($sender,$receiver,h(~delegation),h(~epochs)), CacheStarted($sender,$receiver,~incarnation), SlotObs($sender,$receiver,'held',~incarnation) ]->
  [ Slot($sender,$receiver,'held',~incarnation), Content($sender,$receiver,~delegation,~epochs), Out(<~delegation,~epochs>) ]

rule replace:
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'held',incarnation), Content(sender,receiver,old,oldepochs), Fr(~delegation), Fr(~epochs) ]
  --[ Full(sender,receiver,h(~delegation),h(~epochs)), CacheCurrent(sender,receiver,incarnation), SlotObs(sender,receiver,'held',incarnation) ]->
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'held',incarnation), Content(sender,receiver,~delegation,~epochs), Out(<~delegation,~epochs>) ]

// Restart ends the incarnation holding the cache. No action names it current on
// that step, and the cached pair is dropped: an empty cache holds no content.
rule restart:
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'held',incarnation), Content(sender,receiver,d,e) ]
  --[ Restart(sender,receiver), CacheEnded(sender,receiver,incarnation), SlotObs(sender,receiver,'held',incarnation), SlotObs(sender,receiver,'empty',incarnation) ]->
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'empty',incarnation) ]

// Refill leaves the previous incarnation behind: it observes that slot empty and
// the new one held. It does not emit CacheEmpty for the previous incarnation;
// the record of emptiness belongs to the restart that created it.
rule refill:
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'empty',previous), Fr(~delegation), Fr(~epochs), Fr(~incarnation) ]
  --[ Full(sender,receiver,h(~delegation),h(~epochs)), CacheStarted(sender,receiver,~incarnation), CacheRefilled(sender,receiver,previous,~incarnation,h(~delegation),h(~epochs)), SlotObs(sender,receiver,'empty',previous), SlotObs(sender,receiver,'held',~incarnation) ]->
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'held',~incarnation), Content(sender,receiver,~delegation,~epochs), Out(<~delegation,~epochs>) ]

rule cached:
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'held',incarnation), Content(sender,receiver,d,e), In(<h(d),h(e)>) ]
  --[ Resolved(sender,receiver,h(d),h(e)), CacheCurrent(sender,receiver,incarnation), SlotObs(sender,receiver,'held',incarnation) ]->
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'held',incarnation), Content(sender,receiver,d,e) ]

rule miss:
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'empty',incarnation), In(<dh,eh>) ]
  --[ NeedContext(sender,receiver,dh,eh), CacheEmpty(sender,receiver,incarnation), SlotObs(sender,receiver,'empty',incarnation) ]->
  [ Slot(sender,receiver,'empty',incarnation) ]

// The bridges: each cache action occurs at a step that observes the state it
// names. They hold by construction of the rules, and they are what makes the
// state reachable to a trace formula.
// Non-vacuity, before anything is marked [reuse]: the observed states really
// occur, in the order the protocol produces them, and the cache operations
// themselves are reachable. Without these the invariants below would be
// unreadable as guarantees.
// One pair starts one incarnation.
// Every observation of a slot holding an incarnation traces to a start of it at
// or before that step: initialize emits both at one step, which is why the
// non-strict form is the one that holds. Composed with ended_obs_at_step this
// gives the start of an incarnation that was ended.
// Provenance of the cache-generation actions: what a request saw as current, and
// what a miss found empty, both trace back to an earlier step.
// Lifetime of one incarnation, stated over the state observations: an action
// that names it current is supported by a held observation at or before that
// step; a step that ends it is observed holding and leaves it empty; after an
// end or an empty observation the slot is never observed holding it again.
// The action-level consequences: no request finds an incarnation current after
// it ended or after the cache was seen empty for it, and no current action
// precedes that incarnation's end.
// Two history claims stay open, and neither is refuted: the refill that starts a
// new incarnation follows the restart that emptied the cache, and a resolution
// after a restart follows a delivery. Both quantify over which earlier step
// produced the state now acted on rather than over the state at the acting
// step, so the bridges above do not reach them. The second also names a
// delivered pair, which this theory records only as an action.
// Every resolution traces to an earlier delivery of that pair.
lemma current_obs_at_step [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #i. CacheCurrent(s,r,incarnation) @i ==> SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @i"
lemma empty_obs_at_step [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #i. CacheEmpty(s,r,incarnation) @i ==> SlotObs(s,r,'empty',incarnation) @i"
lemma ended_obs_at_step [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #i. CacheEnded(s,r,incarnation) @i ==> SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @i"
lemma started_obs_at_step [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #i. CacheStarted(s,r,incarnation) @i ==> SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @i"
lemma resolved_obs_at_step [use_induction]:
  "All s r dh eh #i. Resolved(s,r,dh,eh) @i ==> (Ex inc. SlotObs(s,r,'held',inc) @i)"

lemma w_obs_held [use_induction]:
  exists-trace "Ex s r inc #t. SlotObs(s,r,'held',inc) @t"
lemma w_obs_empty [use_induction]:
  exists-trace "Ex s r inc #t. SlotObs(s,r,'empty',inc) @t"
lemma w_both_obs [use_induction]:
  exists-trace "Ex s r inc #k #t. SlotObs(s,r,'held',inc) @k & SlotObs(s,r,'empty',inc) @t & #k < #t"
lemma honest_cached: exists-trace
  "Ex s r d e #i. Resolved(s,r,d,e) @i"
lemma restart_miss: exists-trace
  "Ex s r d e #i #j. Restart(s,r) @i & NeedContext(s,r,d,e) @j & #i < #j"
lemma restart_refill_resolves_witness: exists-trace
  "Ex s r old new d e #i #j #k. Restart(s,r) @i & CacheEnded(s,r,old) @i & CacheRefilled(s,r,old,new,d,e) @j & Resolved(s,r,d,e) @k & CacheCurrent(s,r,new) @k & #i < #j & #j < #k"

lemma cache_incarnation_unique:
  "All s r s2 r2 incarnation #i #j. CacheStarted(s,r,incarnation) @i & CacheStarted(s2,r2,incarnation) @j ==> #i = #j"

lemma held_obs_has_start [use_induction, reuse]:
  "All s r incarnation #t. SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @t ==> (Ex #j. CacheStarted(s,r,incarnation) @j & (#j < #t | #j = #t))"
lemma cache_incarnation_end_has_start:
  "All s r incarnation #i. CacheEnded(s,r,incarnation) @i ==> (Ex #j. CacheStarted(s,r,incarnation) @j & #j < #i)"

lemma cache_incarnation_source [use_induction, reuse]:
  "All s r incarnation #i. CacheCurrent(s,r,incarnation) @i ==> (Ex #j. CacheStarted(s,r,incarnation) @j & #j < #i)"
lemma empty_incarnation_end_source [use_induction, reuse]:
  "All s r incarnation #i. CacheEmpty(s,r,incarnation) @i ==> (Ex #j. CacheEnded(s,r,incarnation) @j & #j < #i)"

lemma current_observes_held [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #i. CacheCurrent(s,r,incarnation) @i ==> (Ex #t. SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @t & (#t < #i | #t = #i))"
lemma empty_obs_after_end [use_induction, reuse]:
  "All s r incarnation #c. CacheEnded(s,r,incarnation) @c ==> SlotObs(s,r,'empty',incarnation) @c"

// Two forms of "an incarnation observed empty or ended is never observed held
// again". Neither is proved: with neither statement available as a source both
// exhaust the search (exit 137 at 8 GiB, 1200 s), while each one verifies only
// when the other stands above it as a [reuse] source - a lemma's statement is
// injected into later proofs whether or not that lemma itself was proved, so
// those two verdicts are conditional on an open goal, not proofs. The pair is
// therefore kept open and WITHOUT [reuse]: no verified verdict below may rest on
// either. Proving them needs a stronger simultaneous induction than this theory
// currently states, not more time or memory. A single combined form with a
// disjunctive antecedent does not parse (unguarded #i).
lemma no_held_obs_after_empty [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #i #t. SlotObs(s,r,'empty',incarnation) @i & SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @t ==> not (#i < #t)"

// Non-vacuity of no_held_obs_after_empty: its antecedent is satisfiable, so that lemma is a
// real obligation and not an empty statement. Generated from it by
// contrib/ci/vacuity-probes.py (exists-trace of the antecedent alone, the
// conclusion's ordering removed - with the ordering the search does not finish).
lemma Nonvac_no_held_obs_after_empty: exists-trace
  "Ex s r incarnation #i #t. SlotObs(s,r,'empty',incarnation) @i & SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @t"
// The same claim read over end actions instead of empty observations. It follows
// from the lemma above plus empty_obs_after_end (restart emits both at one step),
// so with that statement available as a [reuse] source it verifies; with nothing
// assumed it exhausts the search (exit 137 at 8 GiB, 1100-1200 s). Reported open,
// and not usable as a source by anything below: a conditional result resting on an
// open goal is not a proof. Read the pair the other way round: the empty-observation
// form is strictly stronger, because refill emits an empty observation for the
// previous incarnation without any end action, so no end-only invariant covers it.
lemma no_held_obs_after_end [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #c #t. CacheEnded(s,r,incarnation) @c & SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @t ==> not (#c < #t)"

// Non-vacuity of no_held_obs_after_end: its antecedent is satisfiable, so that lemma is a
// real obligation and not an empty statement. Generated from it by
// contrib/ci/vacuity-probes.py (exists-trace of the antecedent alone, the
// conclusion's ordering removed - with the ordering the search does not finish).
lemma Nonvac_no_held_obs_after_end: exists-trace
  "Ex s r incarnation #c #t. CacheEnded(s,r,incarnation) @c & SlotObs(s,r,'held',incarnation) @t"
lemma empty_incarnation_not_current_afterward [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #i #j. CacheEmpty(s,r,incarnation) @i & CacheCurrent(s,r,incarnation) @j ==> not (#i < #j)"
lemma cache_incarnation_active [use_induction]:
  "All s r incarnation #i #j. CacheCurrent(s,r,incarnation) @i & CacheEnded(s,r,incarnation) @j ==> not (#j < #i)"

// A refill only happens against a slot a restart emptied. Stated with the single
// action it is about in the antecedent. The previous form quantified over two
// starts and never named the refill step, and it exhausted the search at every
// setting tried (exit 137 at 8 GiB, 400-700 s) while this one verifies in 141 s.
// The search space, not the memory ceiling, was the obstacle.
lemma refill_follows_prior_restart [use_induction]:
  "All s r previous current d e #i.
     CacheRefilled(s,r,previous,current,d,e) @i
     ==> (Ex #j. Restart(s,r) @j & #j < #i)"
lemma no_resolution_after_restart_without_refill [use_induction]:
  "All s r d e #i #j. Restart(s,r) @i & Resolved(s,r,d,e) @j & #i < #j ==> (Ex d2 e2 #k. Full(s,r,d2,e2) @k & #i < #k & #k < #j)"

lemma cache_origin [use_induction]:
  "All s r d e #i. Resolved(s,r,d,e) @i ==> (Ex #j. Full(s,r,d,e) @j & #j < #i)"
end
